unzip: keep a 0xff byte in a name, as the other 8-bit bytes (homescoop#602).
mapname() let 128..254 through and dropped 255, so rep\xff1.txt was
written as rep1.txt with rc 0. Kept, a name that is not UTF-8 reaches
the realm's path decoding, which refuses it with EILSEQ: unzip reports
"cannot create" and exits non-zero instead of renaming the entry.

--- a/unix/unix.c
+++ b/unix/unix.c
@@ -610,7 +610,7 @@
                  * else allow 8-bit characters (e.g. UTF-8) in filenames:
                  */
                 if (uO.cflxflag ||
-                    (isprint(workch) || (128 <= workch && workch <= 254)))
+                    (isprint(workch) || (128 <= workch && workch <= 255)))
                     *pp++ = (char)workch;
         } /* end switch */
 
